</span></div></summary><div class="sc-empmoP ka-dQLX pf-388_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-OIPVh bgvKDN pf-389_"><p class="sc-zmgRN ebFAfi pf-390_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-2d3a4d5a-c05c-4dfc-b360-a32c6da458e5"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content "><strong>Important Before First Use: Maximizing the Hybrid Technology</strong><br><br>The seasoning process is essential to activate your pan's titanium, optimizing its non-stick properties and ensuring it lasts a lifetime. Follow these instructions before first use and periodically for maintenance.
<br><br><strong>1. Initial Cleaning</strong>
<br><br>Before seasoning, remove any manufacturing residue.
Wash the pan with warm water and mild soap.
Use a soft sponge.
Critical step — drying: Dry the pan immediately with a soft cloth.
Do not let it air dry, to avoid mineral stains.
<br><br><strong>2. Seasoning Procedure (Step by Step)</strong><br><br>To seal the surface and create the final protective layer:
<br><br><strong>1 – Coating</strong>: Pour 1–2 teaspoons of high smoke point oil (sunflower, corn, or canola) onto the dry surface.<br><strong>2 – Spreading</strong>: Using a paper towel, spread the oil across the entire interior, making sure to cover both the steel ridges and the non-stick valleys.
<br><strong>3 – Heat Treatment</strong>: Heat the pan over medium-low heat for 2 to 3 minutes.
<br><strong>4 – Smoke Point:</strong> As soon as you see a light wisp of smoke, remove from heat. Don't let the oil burn or darken.
<br><strong>5 – Cooling</strong>: Let the pan cool to room temperature. Never use cold water to cool it down, as thermal shock can damage the metal's structure.
<br><strong>6 – Finishing</strong>: Once cool, wipe off any excess oil with a clean paper towel.
<br><br><strong>Usage and Performance Guide<br></strong><br><strong>Heat Management</strong>: Thanks to its triple-layer core, these pans distribute heat with extreme efficiency. Always cook on medium or low heat — medium heat on a hybrid pan is equivalent to high heat on a conventional pan.
<br><br><strong>Utensils</strong>: Although its reinforced coating allows the use of metal spatulas, we recommend silicone or wooden utensils to keep the mirror-polish finish looking good for longer.
<br><br><strong>Cleaning</strong>: After cooking, let the pan cool down before washing. If food residue is stuck on, you can soak it in soapy water — the honeycomb technology will loosen the residue without the need for hard scrubbing.</span></p></div></div></div></details><details class="sc-SrAaV fTsMaP pf-393_" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content.Wrapper"><summary><div class="sc-bdOgOc hZBVbi pf-394_ pf-anchor pf-header-item-wrapper" data-header-id="c05c5dfc-3360-432c-ada4-58e599c12ebd" data-active="false" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Header"><svg class="pf-accordion-icon pfa-chevron-right pfa-arrow" style="width:auto;fill:currentcolor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 512"><path d="M278.6 233.4c12.5 12.5 12.5 32.8 0 45.3l-160 160c-12.5 12.5-32.8 12.5-45.3 0s-12.5-32.8 0-45.3L210.7 256 73.4 118.6c-12.5-12.5-12.5-32.8 0-45.3s32.8-12.5 45.3 0l160 160z"></path></svg><span>Why Choose Titanium Technology?

</span></div></summary><div class="sc-empmoP ka-dQLX pf-396_ pf-accordion-body" data-pf-expandable="true" data-pf-type="Accordion3.Content"><div class="pf-accordion-display-content"><div data-pf-type="Accordion3.Flex.Content" class="sc-OIPVh bgvKDN pf-397_"><p class="sc-zmgRN ebFAfi pf-398_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph4"><input type="checkbox" id="compact-3360a32c-6da4-48e5-99c1-2ebdd2b4a0ee"/><span class="pf-paragraph-content ">Cooking on our 100% pure titanium surface guarantees maximum nutrient retention in your food, more than any other cookware. Research shows that titanium surfaces provide the best protection for essential micronutrients, keeping your meals healthier. Unlike traditional pans, which require more water and higher heat, titanium pans and pots help preserve moisture and nutrients.
<br><br>Titanium: The Safest, Most Biocompatible Metal on the Planet
Titanium is the safest metal for human contact. That's why it's trusted for medical implants — it's naturally non-toxic and doesn't react negatively with the body or with food.
<br><br>Traditional non-stick, Teflon-coated pans found in most households, on the other hand, have been linked to cancer-causing chemicals that leach into food. Once ingested, these harmful chemicals — known as "forever chemicals" — remain in the body for life.
<br><br><strong>Naturally Antibacterial
<br></strong>Titanium's natural antibacterial properties make it an excellent choice for medical devices, and it's just as effective in the kitchen. It prevents bacterial growth, keeping your cooking environment safer and healthier, so you can cook with the peace of mind of knowing you're using the cleanest, most hygienic surface available.
<br><br><strong>Unmatched Durability and Heat Resistance<br></strong>Titanium is incredibly durable and withstands extreme temperatures. Whether you're cooking on the stovetop, over an open flame, or in the oven, this pan can handle it all without warping or deteriorating over time. It's built to last, giving you peace of mind with every use.
